+# Clearwater minute approval: a later record, with representation limits
+
+October29,2026. STL01–STL03, CW-B01, B188/H005 and AUD011/AUD016 remain open. A newly located official council-minute entry records a later approval step for the December16,2010 minutes. This is progress in the authorization trail; it does not recover the executed steel-transfer agreement or prove a physical custody event.
+
+## Newly inspected official record
+
+The [January13,2011 Council minute document, page2/item5.1](https://edocuments.myclearwater.com/WebLink/DocView.aspx?id=242633&page=2&dbid=0&repo=Clearwater), reports a motion approving the **December16,2010** minutes as submitted in written summation by the City Clerk, followed by a unanimous vote.
+
+This record is a separately indexed **14-page Council minute document, archive id242633**. It is distinct from the previously acquired **486-page January13 agenda binder, id244540**, which reproduces the December minute copy labelled **Draft / Unapproved**. A targeted Name query found both records and a third, unrelated pension-committee minute record; they were not treated as interchangeable.
+
+The new entry was read in Clearwater's ordinary **View plain text** rendering. The selected passage, source URL, page/item, access date and UTF-8 capture hash are preserved locally and identified in [SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json). That hash identifies a captured text representation, **not an original PDF, historical approved document or signature**. No native/certified minute PDF or authenticated signature/facsimile was acquired. The January entry reports approval; it does not identify the exact historical bytes approved.
+
+## Keep the events and versions separate
+
+The separately indexed [December16 minute text, page10/item9.2](https://edocuments.myclearwater.com/WebLink/DocView.aspx?id=240784&page=10&dbid=0), authorizes the Fire Chief to sign the World Trade Center Steel Transfer Agreement and accept steel from the Port Authority at Hangar17. Its [page12 consent paragraph](https://edocuments.myclearwater.com/WebLink/DocView.aspx?id=240784&page=12&dbid=0) reports unanimous passage. The January entry records later approval of the minutes.
+
+These are different procedural events:
+
+- wording authorizing signature and acceptance;
+- the reported December consent vote;
+- the reported January approval of the written December minutes;
+- agreement execution, release, transport, receipt and cutting, which still require their own records.
+
+The earlier Draft/Unapproved label is retained in [PREVIOUS-CW-B01.json](PREVIOUS-CW-B01.json), with its original observation and published-source link unchanged. We do not relabel that copy, infer that every word of the draft/current viewer text was approved, select a controlling source or determine the legal effect of the records. A later approval entry is not, by itself, evidence that an earlier draft label was false.
+
+The archive displays creation/modification fields for each viewer document. Those fields are preserved as displayed metadata, not authenticated signature or historical approval dates. The December text lacks Draft/Unapproved wording in the inspected representation, but that does not prove absence from its facsimile or authenticate final status.
+
+## Earlier conflicts and missing custody records remain
+
+The held November17,2010 letter has blank signature lines. Earlier comparisons preserve the staff's cutting description, the absence of express cutting permission in the scoped letter, the holds-neither wording versus the letter's affirmative terms, and the missing incorporated December2009 order. This new minute entry resolves none of those questions. [Prior source review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/4b57a56d460bd7ea4b34e9f8771cf5f472d19250/investigation/broader-evidence/steel-clearwater-agreement-2026-10-29/README.md).
+
+Authorization and minute approval cannot substitute for a signed transfer instrument, release/bill of lading, recipient receipt or a cutting/condition record. The record does not establish actual alteration, disposal, present scientific access, physical origin, or a W14A/W14B/C12/Sample1 join. It neither proves nor excludes obstruction elsewhere.
+
+## Acquisition and actual review scope
+
+Selected December viewer pages1,10,12,21 and January pages1–2 were read as text representations. Large source-image tiles failed to render, so the screenshot supplied no signature/status authentication. The normal public viewer's bounded four-page Print export returned HTML, not PDF; its response and failure receipt are preserved locally. That export route stopped without an unchanged retry. The access failure is not a historical anomaly.
+
+One initial line-filter diagnostic also returned an overlong repeated whole-document text string. That was incidental extraction, not a complete manual review or independent source. Subsequent capture bounded only the consent paragraph and its actual page12 link. No full21/14-page image reading is claimed.
+
+[OBSERVATIONS-AND-TODOS.json](OBSERVATIONS-AND-TODOS.json) preserves the narrow findings and remaining originals. [CHECKLIST.json](CHECKLIST.json) accounts for requirements; [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff) records exact additions at a new path. Earlier PDFs, draft observations and public history remain unchanged.
+
+No physical, numerical collapse, specimen, clock or legal-entitlement test was performed. All eighteen original five-track requirements remain unfinished. Missing originals stay TODOs while other available operational-record work proceeds. Raw source text/images/PDFs, signatures, contacts, unrelated personal details, private case correspondence and strategy are excluded from the public payload. Publication verifies reviewed file identity, not historical authenticity or substantive completion.
